    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c723bc6e-4b07-5a73-9cf9-db842f5a3806",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following vector fields are conservative on $\\mathbb R^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $F=(- x \\sin{\\left(2 x y \\right)})\\,i+(- 4 y \\sin{\\left(2 x y \\right)})\\,j$\n- **II.** $G=(8 x - 2)\\,i+(5 y^{2} + 2 y + 1)\\,j$\n- **III.** $H=(8 y^{2})\\,i+(8 x^{2})\\,j$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $F(x,y)=P(x,y)\\,i+Q(x,y)\\,j$ be a vector field with domain $D=\\mathbb R^{2},$ where $P$ and $Q$ have continuous first-order partial derivatives everywhere on $D.$ Then, we have the following theorem:\n\n$F$ *is conservative if and only if $\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}$ everywhere on $D.$*\n\nNote that for each of our functions, $D=\\mathbb R^{2}.$ With this in mind, let's check each of the vector fields.\n\n- For the vector field $F,$ we have $P=- x \\sin{\\left(2 x y \\right)}$ and $Q=- 4 y \\sin{\\left(2 x y \\right)}$. Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=- 2 x^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x y \\right)},\\qquad \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}=- 8 y^{2} \\cos{\\left(2 x y \\right)}.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal everywhere, we conclude that $F$ is not conservative on $\\mathbb R^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $G,$ we have $P=8 x - 2$ and $Q=5 y^{2} + 2 y + 1$. Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=0,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}=0.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are continuous and equal everywhere on $\\mathbb R^{2},$ we conclude that $G$ is conservative on $\\mathbb R^{2}.$\n\n- For the vector field $H,$ we have $P=8 y^{2}$ and $Q=8 x^{2}$. Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=16 y,\\qquad \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}=16 x.\n$$\n\nSince the partial derivatives are not equal everywhere, we conclude that $H$ is not conservative on $\\mathbb R^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
